<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Edward</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Edward is a lake in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albertine-rift">Albertine Rift</a> on the border between Uganda and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a>. Linked by the Kazinga Channel to Lake George, it drains northwards through the Semliki River into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-albert">Lake Albert</a>. The kingdom of Ankole grew up in the grasslands to its east. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-morton-stanley">Henry Morton Stanley</a> named it in 1888 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a>, the future Edward VII.</p></div>
